= G1 Final 2026 — Production Meeting Notes =

* '''Date:''' October 11, 2026 (the catch-up day, morning after the Block B playoff)
* '''Location:''' NOPW head office, Okami
* '''Present:''' Booking office; Marcus Vance; Taumafa (winners' meeting, per tradition — both block winners in the room for the Final pitch)
* '''Re:''' G1 Final 2026 — October 18, Aizawa Dome (30,000, sellout expected)

== The pitch ==

'''The Workhorse vs. The Giant.'''

Vance ran the first perfect block in G1 history — 8-0-1, 17 points, and never said a word doing it. Taumafa lost twice, needed the first playoff in G1 history, and survived the Dragon lariat to get here. The contrast sells itself: the silent Mercian technician against the family's ceremony; the Drill Driver against the Samoan driver; the man who never lost against the man who learned how to.

The winner challenges Leoni Masua for the IGO Heavyweight Championship at Wrestling Summit, January 4, Toyozawa Dome.

'''Finish (locked in the room):''' Vance goes over. 27:44, second Drill Driver. Beats:
# Taumafa dominates the first ten — power, hip attack, corner splash. Vance chops the giant down by the knee, the Ishida blueprint from Day 1 made explicit.
# 22:00 — Vance hits the Drill Driver. Taumafa kicks out at 2.9. First man to kick out of it all tour. Building erupts.
# 25:30 — Taumafa hits the Samoan driver. Vance kicks out at 2.9. First man to survive it. The crowd comes unglued.
# 27:44 — Taumafa goes for the second Samoan driver; Vance slides off the shoulder, 44 Calibre lariat, second Drill Driver, 1-2-3.

'''Post-match (the angle):''' Vance takes a microphone for the first time in his NOPW run. The silence was the whole story — the room agrees the break has to be short, plain, and final. Pitch line: ''"Seventeen points. No words. One more man."'' He points at the hard cam. Leoni's music hits; the champion walks out with the belt and the namo, stands in the ring, says nothing back. Staredown to close the show. Graphic: Wrestling Summit — January 4 — Toyozawa Dome.

'''Taumafa's notes:''' Happy to put Vance over — the family wants the strongest possible man across from the chief at Summit, and the giant's playoff win keeps him made. Asks that the kickout of the Drill Driver be protected (2.9, not 2.5). Agreed.

'''Vance's notes:''' Speaks freely in the office; the silence is for the cameras. Only request — the post-match promo stays under thirty seconds. Agreed.

